  "notes": "Live-band retro-soul/funk pop. Every number here comes off a live-ensemble claim: \"played kit tracked live with a full rhythm section, tight and dry, backbeat hard on 2&4, hi-hat 16ths with an accented offbeat; handclaps and tambourine doubling the backbeat as a period signature.\" So the snare is hard-transient with a short tail, `hihat.base` is 16th with a wide velocity spread and no roll vocabulary, the perc lanes are `tambourine` and `clave` at `downbeat` placement, and the humanize block is the loosest kind this section authors — a band, not a grid. The bass is a co-lead and not an 808: \"fingered or slapped electric bass playing a full syncopated funk line — the bass is a co-lead instrument, not a support\", which is `independent_riff` at `followRootsProb` 0.26 with slap-shaped cells. Harmony is the entry's most unusual claim for this lane: \"one- or two-chord vamps with extended dominants rather than progressions\", so `maxChords` is 2, `harmonicRhythm` is vamp-dominant and `seventh` carries half the weight; \"major-mode funk keys (D, E♭, B♭) with dominant-7th and 9th chords and blues-scale melodic borrowing\" is the key list and the `major_blues` scale weight. \"Toplines are call-and-response with the horns, short-celled, and rhythmically on top of the beat\" is `call_response` with a small motif; the counter is the live horn section, so `answer_lick` carries top weight. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a high-medium rating because \"tempo/key bands inferred\": every drum probability, the humanize numbers, the melody register and the F and G in `session.keys` are INFERRED — the entry names \"major-mode funk keys (D, E♭, B♭)\" and no others. `bpm.mode` 112 is the midpoint of the stated 110—115 funk core.",
